<description>
Recolor each black component according to its size while preserving the grey background.

Input structure:
- The grid has a dominant non-black background color.
- The only foreground pixels are black.
- Each black 4-connected component has area 1, 2, or 3.

Rule:
- Preserve all background pixels.
- Recolor area-1 black components green, area-2 components red, and area-3 components blue.

Key insight:
- The black cells are not independent pixels; each connected blob is classified by its 4-connected area.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "black 4-connected foreground components on a grey background",
  "transform": "preserve the background; recolor each black component by area: size 1 to green, size 2 to red, size 3 to blue"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10x10 [observed]
  background: GREY (5), fills ~72-75% of cells
  foreground: only BLACK (0) in input; only GREEN/RED/BLUE in output
  components:
    definition: 4-connected components of black cells
    count: 15-16 total
    size_1: 6-8 single-pixel components -> recolored GREEN in output
    size_2: 5-6 domino components (horizontal or vertical) -> recolored RED in output
    size_3: 2-4 triomino components (any 4-connected shape) -> recolored BLUE in output
    allowed_sizes: exactly {1, 2, 3}; no other sizes
    total_black_pixels: 25-28
    adjacency: distinct components may be 8-adjacent but never 4-adjacent
  transform: recolor each black component by its area (1->GREEN, 2->RED, 3->BLUE)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct random placement
  steps:
    1. Create 10x10 grid filled with GREY.
    2. Choose component counts: size-1 in [6,8], size-2 in [5,6], size-3 in [2,4].
    3. Generate all components as polyomino shapes (size-1 is a dot; size-2 is
       horizontal or vertical domino; size-3 is any of the two free triominoes -
       L-shape or I-shape - in any rotation).
    4. Place components one at a time on the grid. For each, pick a random anchor
       and check that all cells are empty (GREY) and no cell is 4-adjacent to an
       existing black cell (8-adjacent is allowed). Place largest first for easier
       packing. Retry placement if constraint violated.
    5. All placed cells become BLACK. The output is derived by recoloring each
       component per the size->color mapping.
```
</generation_spec>
